#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128946 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/id #uuid "b4697448-d5f7-59ae-86a1-689ae00ebb73" :question/math-academy-id "e-7197" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/1d180fd5de88ebc465df522879142e5a4c5446c758aaccde792092968078c254.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the curves $x=2y^3-2y$ and  $x=y^3-4y,$ and the $y$-axis, as shown in the picture. Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm{d}A.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/6812e8036df171e162bee49d2edcff6d4a742e7bb4f14247713bd2332c64ccc6.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq y  \\leq 0, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^3\\!-\\!4y \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y  \\leq 1, \\quad 2y^3\\!-\\!2y \\leq x \\leq 0 \\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{3}-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y-2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}-2{y}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128947 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "9a106b26-c6fe-5e4b-ae43-9cc02ddb67c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7198" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y= 2^x,$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $x=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/b80527fdef6f890581b8f56431e1b72a8f7eae3b41827caa16486ed9f2fd45ea.png)" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/939e46b3ed4266f3c18d3567f951276e420292781cfc414711c244f453bc4029.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2^x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq x  \\leq 4, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{2}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "be10aba9-930e-54c3-814d-8d089757affc" :question/math-academy-id "e-7199" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=2+\\ln x,$  and the lines $y=1$, $x=1,$ and  $x=e,$  as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/4b0dff15fa9fa93ed61183702bff6bb443daf14b0adbf56cf4b97e3bd830ceea.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/2228ad860fea1e2c30d20bce749f654da02a97c65fd5e70152a07761e26f3e78.png)\n\n    \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y  \\leq 2, \\quad 1 \\leq x \\leq e \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 2 \\leq y  \\leq 3, \\quad e^{y-2} \\leq x \\leq e\\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{y-2}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "508bdf93-8eb5-59be-b79c-263552dd6348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{-2x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368884} {:answer/id #uuid "1aa0e36f-722b-50e3-a646-719b1dd482f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368885} {:answer/id #uuid "96bd9871-6319-56ee-b0b3-1a1911e4aaa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368886} {:answer/id #uuid "0a440729-dc6c-5993-88e4-f68d2c02c029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{4x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368887} {:answer/id #uuid "41358bee-8b70-56cf-847c-630f37ddbc72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{-2x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{4x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96bd9871-6319-56ee-b0b3-1a1911e4aaa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368886} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ef0fbe2-c555-56be-a2d1-ce9c7e5b30a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7aeb314a-1c40-56e8-9c79-581f6c42093d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132290" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/797cddb4ea3cb41959df88e56517e9ee71e76e3cd08a9a93d2957b9792d14abb.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-\\frac{2x}{3},$ $y=\\frac{4x}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{x}{3}+3,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/0e69b1cb480b87216273db4336adff57cbf9d9bc450aac4b0cdb58b1ae63f6f7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,-\\frac{2x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{4x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "525fd8e3-926f-5961-882f-ea53f19a4fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368891} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9f7084-40aa-5cd2-adcc-6e89e912c139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{2}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368892} {:answer/id #uuid "fd47ecb6-5a10-5a07-91dd-80e8b79325a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{x/2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368893} {:answer/id #uuid "35179304-8925-5da6-8bf2-193bed024c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368894} {:answer/id #uuid "a1370157-41e4-57d6-8c0b-322c7ef4d70d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "525fd8e3-926f-5961-882f-ea53f19a4fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368891} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fba3a7a-123d-57b2-bdcd-2020283f8a59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9666ae8-02f3-5bcc-8118-4503675d1849" :question/math-academy-id "q-132291" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=2$ and $y=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/990f2180e92ffa9ae0b77a7c8c4aae284cacf03f7a7a62b1ed0b56f24705d671.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/db7fe0aa7b746eab86c011545ec37d59d8f225f02a9fc6f4388754e1c528db8c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}x\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e2b1a5b-0afd-51d1-b78f-19d89622ce20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368898} {:answer/id #uuid "8c555b30-698b-5508-91ae-8a5b523368fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368899} {:answer/id #uuid "629caba4-f2c8-5694-9b2f-6262758c871b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368900} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d0848c-1259-5a5e-a940-79f1fec2ec2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368901} {:answer/id #uuid "1d5e940a-18d6-5803-9bf7-4372db8fb2ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d0848c-1259-5a5e-a940-79f1fec2ec2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368901} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ead9de1-ec2f-5964-af1d-fd2d935607b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce4cc95b-9711-5123-b41c-4c736729a64b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132292" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2,$ and the lines $y=x+2,$ $x=-2$ and $x=2.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/019f0f9f83ddf323d543d109677335cb3ae72a200baf834453a0eca16a9353ba.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/d222e86f6af7c3ed2b35711114c9062d6f0c9b0f2551aa44cac33318c6e5813f.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,x+2\\le y\\le \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\le y\\le x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a211c1d-44e2-53eb-a40c-2afe07c65a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2-y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368905} {:answer/id #uuid "04609af8-1b21-57b5-8205-603182f6b744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368906} {:answer/id #uuid "fccd1a97-5e4a-5a93-969a-98227ab66ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{-\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368907} {:answer/id #uuid "aa87ef4e-5709-5f34-a494-a0d8a14fbb16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368908} {:answer/id #uuid "87531304-de0a-54be-9266-2b02f7001467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2-y}^{-\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04609af8-1b21-57b5-8205-603182f6b744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368906} :answer-field/id #uuid "a79ee524-8165-55bb-bd18-8e520d9464e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a88b2724-df79-5926-a981-b520191fb2e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132385" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/a4515d2789a9b5c7a08210c0ef2611e7b6e661850b1fa822016b880427088bae.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2},$ and the lines $y=2-x$ and $y=x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=-\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=2-x & \\,⟹\\,x=2-y \\\\ y=x & \\,⟹\\,x=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/78aa61f11856dbf35287a0af016b56744fec354d6c4e64690a1a6fe466f164e8.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,-\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le 2-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc789ae7-6068-54ff-9f22-27223fc51909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368912} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e26f71-a2b3-5439-8629-250bfb81046a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368913} {:answer/id #uuid "38d29830-ca2f-591a-8bf3-c63c8ac04146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368914} {:answer/id #uuid "7e444c51-1c17-5ac2-9d31-afb3f75b2448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368915} {:answer/id #uuid "5e14e716-f454-566d-8e11-a60bd9dc04a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e444c51-1c17-5ac2-9d31-afb3f75b2448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368915} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a89ae5-5dfb-5651-9740-fcdca2c0b229" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cd98531c-9c3a-58d9-a39c-eb25bb6f031c" :question/math-academy-id "q-132391" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={e}^{x},$ and the lines $y=1-x$ and $x=1.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={e}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/0c61de3680b68dcf16267483fe1a51f0ef0e4c8247104215ae319d6c01b7a571.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c2a3cd01f74a2adb96e13212916dbb1b4476040d701ccd755258bd22fdefa5de.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1-y\\le x\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\le x\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71db9016-b8a1-538e-a7e2-e2d0c69a67a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368919} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf0dd73-9a46-568c-9491-2b69fc43e4ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368920} {:answer/id #uuid "705abc50-237c-56ce-8f6a-c617f48bb020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368921} {:answer/id #uuid "1f89cfc2-4bc8-5b6c-8c9e-1f150b64653a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{6-4y}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368922} {:answer/id #uuid "c975e734-6b56-55ba-8ebe-bc059d4599c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71db9016-b8a1-538e-a7e2-e2d0c69a67a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368919} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ae2c67-5924-52d5-a137-61bd2cd2965b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf42f9c9-2acd-54b4-a37d-2acf279d635d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132397" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=6-4x$ and $y=2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-x & \\,⟹\\,x=-y \\\\ y=6-4x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4} \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/08237d1ca2e01d0cf620dfa06a4265d8053b7ee34d0b65036aad7d5734726e1c.png)\n\n \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c756dc7924fc4c116601da907eb3b767b8a40647e063c146dad83b0ea660933b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d712e608-39fa-53d3-99d0-4c7b613f7c82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368926} {:answer/id #uuid "59e551d3-cc68-5d06-9e3d-938b3ec6eeab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368927} {:answer/id #uuid "098809cb-ae5c-57fb-8d4f-d5971c2a9b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368928} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b588a4-6813-5252-907d-7241cde00cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368929} {:answer/id #uuid "eaba30a1-03f3-5225-a164-814bae7b3995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "098809cb-ae5c-57fb-8d4f-d5971c2a9b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368928} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2fa8e2e-27dd-53f6-9fa5-caef34f379da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98fde332-e10f-5706-8291-a4bf10d842e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-132423" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/a4265e8993b5c7ea5756fe55facd5313e5c2237cbdbc851195ebf458e5246060.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/33a38da74b282f0ec1fb2fae9cb155feb2a5fd39128c7607b80c6b84fedd29b4.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 3-x}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,3-x\\le y\\le x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x-1}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{3-x}^{x-1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{x-1}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{3-x}^{x-1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}[(x-1)^{2}-(3-x)^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(8-4x)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(4x-8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(8x-2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{2}+(2{x}^{2}-8x){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(2-1)-2({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})+2({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})-8(4-2) \\\\  & =8-6+24-16 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99a9e816-28e8-56f3-beb0-f84570f18f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y - 6}^{y/3}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127113} {:answer/id #uuid "b32a7d48-37b0-5d6e-9093-0756a97cef84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{6 - y}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y/2}^{y/3}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127114} {:answer/id #uuid "df24c72c-7874-571d-95cd-c83af5cc06c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127115} {:answer/id #uuid "e5e2debd-3524-5015-9348-c1930de0e879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127116} {:answer/id #uuid "78030bc8-8d41-503d-b6c4-f8acdc3741f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{y - 6}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y/3}^{y - 6}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5e2debd-3524-5015-9348-c1930de0e879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127116} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e11bd0-c56d-528e-9571-41f1adad3049" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75185755-8578-56f9-bff0-716550a71de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-37757" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/3fb6039f0a1de69d41644d7153d205062e85cdfce7cdb6b6270d952f2dbab6c3.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=x+6,$ $y=2x,$ and $y=3x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y=x+6 & \\,⟹\\,x=y-6 \\\\ y=3x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c453d46a1f0cd6e6ddfa926de471fe38663df2bd86b9cdf4e58ce8d42462774a.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 9,\\,\\frac{y}{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,9\\le y\\le 12,\\,y-6\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0bbe2af-9d09-51e5-adba-f0b49a28ba82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1+x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e+x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368933} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ce1c0e-6121-5bfc-aafa-62d26a83a333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368934} {:answer/id #uuid "65bf628d-dba1-5661-947b-7b5bb930c8f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368935} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad46bcf-8381-55d3-85fe-2dd85e06a1ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e+x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368936} {:answer/id #uuid "3a89703a-7e06-5b6a-9932-35678d8b5a37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65bf628d-dba1-5661-947b-7b5bb930c8f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368935} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0d6ca8-8cd2-5a5f-b12a-468115e606ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb21676e-08c7-5934-b467-875d09f0ef3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82074" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={e}^{x},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$  and the lines $y=1-x$  and $y=1+e-x.$ \nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/4854afc35aff7cfb47ba09481f975b22e41f3309b08a2ba7c409a4bbd32c8601.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/50c5b7a864099f512515ab2db4c1596382883e93f7d4b23b9d16b91e42e3021b.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 1+e-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae8a186f-9167-5a80-9dda-2d9e8aa2ba7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}^{4}{\\int }_{{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368940} {:answer/id #uuid "a3607d52-792c-5ea8-a8c7-224cba16f32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368941} {:answer/id #uuid "79995432-87ba-5cf3-b7fa-1e0e4a2c82b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}{\\int }_{2}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}^{4}{\\int }_{{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368942} {:answer/id #uuid "6addd573-a9b0-5c7f-b48e-735975050ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368943} {:answer/id #uuid "62d3ac6b-1b58-52b0-ad10-1a111cde2664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3607d52-792c-5ea8-a8c7-224cba16f32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368941} :answer-field/id #uuid "013b6830-3c84-51bc-8e87-b87591928ab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5b241a60-d8fd-5bf0-9caf-5547e75ebf63" :question/math-academy-id "q-82137" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={2}^{x},$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $y=1$ and $y=6-x.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={2}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={log}_{2}⁡y \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2} \\\\ y=6-x & \\,⟹\\,x=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe95bc4ca8c687c79fe1c475eb1d8001d71a41ba34e076ad7fdfa8391cb08839.png)\n\n   \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/099c35cbab4dfdd4a94207ed950fbdca8b8e766a612fb5e665e7d443d75ec050.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,{log}_{2}⁡y\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 4,\\,{log}_{2}⁡y\\le x\\le 6-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420d2f05-4dc3-5b9f-a4f5-d45f9401d57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368947} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3c2501-e46c-5969-a051-950d46653d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368948} {:answer/id #uuid "43a8cbc1-fbc7-5ead-847c-e34b61988a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368949} {:answer/id #uuid "87b0d9e4-62bf-56a0-afc1-7180317b7cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368950} {:answer/id #uuid "b9271914-7718-5fac-a491-9c3528f0f523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "420d2f05-4dc3-5b9f-a4f5-d45f9401d57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368947} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0120ab-aa95-51ed-8ee1-dbad7f59f2f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "436c8a72-dab1-585b-85dc-3a344114e654" :question/math-academy-id "q-82223" :question/problem "${∬}_{|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}\\,\\,6(x+y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c9072d2b8f1b49770403280af13d3d8e681247f168e796c056eb697fe28b8ba9.png)\n\n  \n\nThe  region $D={(x,y)|\\,\\,|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}$ can be  partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/d16296029378c7adb891affba63683971ff972b5ed0268641ac3b677c694b5f8.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le 2-y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le y+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}6(x+y)^{2}\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}6(x+y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}6(x+y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}6(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{y+2}6(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3(x+y)^{2}]_{y}^{2-y}\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[3(x+y)^{2}]_{-y}^{y+2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3(4-4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3(2y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3{[4y-\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1}+4{[(y+1)^{3}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =8+4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96bd6456-1c50-50ec-9299-af511d678379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{78}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368954} {:answer/id #uuid "4717a8f1-7cde-50a9-bc5f-ed423f37adbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368955} {:answer/id #uuid "74763c02-2a94-5520-ac2f-fd98170a1c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368956} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d04c91-ee9c-55d1-aca3-aea23efc376d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368957} {:answer/id #uuid "521ab99a-f7b0-52b3-bf38-cbff26aefe20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{106}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74763c02-2a94-5520-ac2f-fd98170a1c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368956} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c9084e-dcce-5597-82b6-de8e535380f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3dcdfeb1-c7df-5260-bb38-cfc091e51c68" :question/math-academy-id "q-82229" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/ebb0b09ffab6ffdff6a04104b09d6904302fdb7580262663b5e0c65bd3f95502.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curve $y=(x-1)^{2}$ and the lines $y=x+1$ and $y=3-x,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/f26c3e1bbbc268308db8d419bc799ad5349673e97c8828471997a5d36cb94d7d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le 3-x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+1)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1}+{[-\\frac{(3-x)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =((\\frac{8}{3}-0)-(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}))+((-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-(-\\frac{8}{3}-0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}+\\frac{32}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f4f08e-c1f1-578a-b36b-a2f91a43caeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368961} {:answer/id #uuid "4c5ffa47-dcbb-5d71-8aa4-25185c7285cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368962} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5629ae-9c80-548d-a66c-815c9e50d338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368963} {:answer/id #uuid "743720b2-5ee9-5e2f-b742-3ef3aa2d0829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368964} {:answer/id #uuid "9cbb48d3-a416-533a-906d-5d61bd9c3c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a5629ae-9c80-548d-a66c-815c9e50d338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368963} :answer-field/id #uuid "c13c3b64-0d06-5b45-8774-5371a6d897ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13e33bff-8759-571b-aca8-15a30bd49e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82355" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=-6{x}^{2}+24x-17$ and lines $y=6x-5,$ $x=3,$ and $y=1.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe0209b3ed99aae4a1a939dfc7a8e0e400976809cc220abb1fbdf2f766c76171.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c8ba7d6923e2e4ef9ee528c48a8f5664ec10e4f05a13dad941713600d93ddfe5.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 6x-5}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le -6{x}^{2}+24x-17}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028be94a-72c2-5f0e-ae1e-ed4916e6b1c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368968} {:answer/id #uuid "f81f41a8-8294-5051-90f1-b8c9edf5901f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368969} {:answer/id #uuid "c0caca54-652d-5656-8be2-c80e091f86f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368970} {:answer/id #uuid "90ae483c-4995-55a9-a506-d6c35df47cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368971} {:answer/id #uuid "5825effa-fe41-5333-b60f-701fb3285424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5825effa-fe41-5333-b60f-701fb3285424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368972} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d825b63-fc7e-5f47-8f54-0cdec494c88d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4837c157-fc9f-5c75-9787-2e74e7f04e9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-82360" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/ad8d4069ab0effd57ba58ccc4bf5792d5a014b114afb086e6d4b71d69ba14d2c.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=|x|,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/2fcb30778db2f051a7a819ae701808af59ac18d27c25a9c57ce678caa6c3ee3b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le -x}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2x\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2x\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2x[-x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x[x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{-1}^{0}+{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((0-(-\\frac{2}{3}(-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{4}))+((\\frac{2}{3}(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{4})-0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d5d7b4-92d0-5d12-8b5f-75003cc00036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368975} {:answer/id #uuid "f18c82a9-1cb1-5cb8-b245-75c59bba119f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368976} {:answer/id #uuid "f925ff97-d190-5786-b8d9-828a96695dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368977} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc9f465-6e80-59d5-b200-58948c3c4af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368978} {:answer/id #uuid "9f70567f-4733-5682-bebf-635ba3231e8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc9f465-6e80-59d5-b200-58948c3c4af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368978} :answer-field/id #uuid "25abd9bc-6970-541f-ab75-8f0cb65594b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "964b4bf4-f010-55d7-af2e-96cfe4a3d003" :question/math-academy-id "q-82362" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/13275042f8b7b74e394b3cee1350c19cfa50ddf63899066682cbd0109f42d6bf.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/648121ff2a676f6a472a6e221dffe813eca55f914aed0ca9a285bb0d4cd81ab3.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get \n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}4xy\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}4xy\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(9-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}2x(9-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}16x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}18x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}+9{x}^{2}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =8(4-0)+9(9-4) \\\\  & =77.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
